{
  "tema": 5188,
  "slug": "condicional-haber",
  "titulo": "Conjugate haber in the conditional",
  "subtitulo": "Habría: there would be, for one thing or many.",
  "foto": "t08.jpg",
  "regla": "Haber has the conditional stem habr-: habría, habrías, habría, habríamos, habrían. Habría alone means there would be and stays singular.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Haber** is irregular in the conditional: add the regular conditional endings to the stem **habr-**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "**habr-**",
            "**-ía, -ías, -ía, -íamos, -ían**"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "haber"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "habría"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "habrías"
            ],
            [
              "él, ella, usted",
              "habría"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "habríamos"
            ],
            [
              "ustedes, ellos",
              "habrían"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "On its own, **habría** means _there would be_. It stays **singular**, whether one thing or many things follow: **habría mucha gente**, **habría muchos carros**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: like **hay** and **habrá**, **habría** never goes plural when it means _there would be_."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Habría== mucha gente en ese festival.",
              "en": "There would be a lot of people at that festival."
            },
            {
              "es": "En ese pueblo ==habría== casas muy viejas.",
              "en": "In that town there would be very old houses."
            },
            {
              "es": "No ==habría== mucho que hacer en Tecate.",
              "en": "There wouldn't be much to do in Tecate."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Habría== mucha neblina en la mañana.",
              "en": "There would be a lot of fog in the morning."
            },
            {
              "es": "No ==habría== demasiado tráfico en la carretera.",
              "en": "There wouldn't be too much traffic on the highway."
            },
            {
              "es": "Sin el huerto, no ==habría== tomates en el barrio.",
              "en": "Without the garden, there would be no tomatoes in the neighborhood."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
